From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DFS: Complete AP setup with driver-managed DFS

MTK AP SME with DFS offload manages radar detection in the driver.
hostapd's DFS-required check can prevent AP setup from following this
driver-managed path.

Bypass that check for MTK AP SME with DFS offload and complete pending
AP setup when a channel notification arrives.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/dfs.c
+++ b/src/ap/dfs.c
@@ -1539,6 +1539,10 @@ int hostapd_is_dfs_required(struct hosta
 {
 	int n_chans, n_chans1, start_chan_idx, start_chan_idx1, res;
 
+	if ((iface->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MTK_AP_SME) &&
+	    (iface->drv_flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_DFS_OFFLOAD))
+		return 0;
+
 	if ((!(iface->drv_flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_DFS_OFFLOAD) &&
 	     !iface->conf->ieee80211h) ||
 	    !iface->current_mode ||
--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -1422,7 +1422,8 @@ void hostapd_event_ch_switch(struct host
 		hostapd_ubus_notify_csa(hapd, freq);
 	} else if (hapd->iface->drv_flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_DFS_OFFLOAD) {
 		/* Complete AP configuration for the first bring up. */
-		if (is_dfs0 > 0 &&
+		if ((is_dfs0 > 0 ||
+		     (hapd->iface->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MTK_AP_SME)) &&
 		    hostapd_is_dfs_required(hapd->iface) <= 0 &&
 		    hapd->iface->state != HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED) {
 			/* Fake a CAC start bit to skip setting channel */
